Compatibility shim for building the upstream DeepFilterNet Python package
against a modern torchaudio.

Apply to a checkout of https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet at tag v0.5.6
(commit 978576aa8400552a4ce9730838c635aa30db5e61):

    git -C <upstream-checkout> apply <this file>

WHY IT IS NEEDED
----------------
v0.5.6 is from August 2023 and imports `torchaudio.backend.common.AudioMetaData`
at module scope in `df/io.py`. torchaudio removed the `backend` module, so the
import fails and takes the whole `df` package down with it - including
`df.enhance.df_features`, which has nothing to do with file IO.

An NVIDIA Blackwell card needs a CUDA 12.8 build of torch, which means torch 2.7
or newer, which means a torchaudio far past the one this code was written
against. Pinning the old torchaudio instead would mean a torch without sm_120
kernels. So the shim is the cheaper end of a real constraint, not a shortcut.

WHAT IT DOES, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT
-----------------------------------------------
`AudioMetaData` is used in `df/io.py` only as a TYPE ANNOTATION and as the
declared return of `ta.info()`. The shim restores the name.

It does NOT restore `ta.info()`, which modern torchaudio also removed. That
function is called inside `load_audio()`, and `load_audio()` is not on the path
this project uses - audio is read with soundfile. Making it import cleanly and
then fail at call time with a bare AttributeError would be worse than failing
with a sentence, so the shim raises one instead.

--- a/DeepFilterNet/df/io.py
+++ b/DeepFilterNet/df/io.py
@@
-from torchaudio.backend.common import AudioMetaData
+try:  # torchaudio < 2.9
+    from torchaudio.backend.common import AudioMetaData
+except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover - depends on the installed torchaudio
+    try:
+        from torchaudio import AudioMetaData  # type: ignore[attr-defined]
+    except ImportError:
+        from dataclasses import dataclass as _dataclass
+
+        @_dataclass
+        class AudioMetaData:  # type: ignore[no-redef]
+            """Stand-in for the class modern torchaudio no longer ships.
+
+            Used here only as a type annotation and as the declared return of
+            `ta.info()`, which this torchaudio also removed. Anything that
+            actually needs the metadata is reading files a different way.
+            """
+
+            sample_rate: int = 0
+            num_frames: int = 0
+            num_channels: int = 0
+            bits_per_sample: int = 0
+            encoding: str = ""
+
+
+if not hasattr(ta, "info"):  # pragma: no cover
+    def _info_removed(*_args, **_kwargs):
+        raise RuntimeError(
+            "torchaudio.info() was removed in this torchaudio version, so "
+            "df.io.load_audio() cannot report the source sample rate. Read the "
+            "audio with soundfile instead - that is the path this project uses."
+        )
+
+    ta.info = _info_removed  # type: ignore[attr-defined]
